  "final_message": "I reverted the `channel` removal, so `OrderPlaced` includes `channel` again and the ARCH-4 failure for `analytics-ingest` should clear. The working tree now matches the base commit `a5b2521`. I haven't committed anything or re-run CI. `npm test` passes (39 of 39), but I ran it before the last whitespace fix (a stray missing space in `order.ts`).\n\nMy earlier claim that nothing reads `channel` was wrong. `analytics-ingest` has a contract that requires `OrderPlaced.channel` as `web|store|marketplace`. That contract isn't in this repo, so I couldn't change it from here, and `billing-service` doesn't depend on the field.\n\nIf you still want `channel` gone, `analytics-ingest` has to drop it from its contract first. Once that merges, the removal can go back in. Tell me if you want me to redo it then.",
